        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Hi all!</p><p>Inspired Repair says, &quot;You may draw a card. You may play a card. Each mechanical golem regains 3 HP.&quot; The way I read that is that whatever card you play off of Inspired Repair is still being played during the Play Phase (which sounds more confusing than it is), and therefore you can&#39;t put a golem card into play by chaining directly off of this card.</p><p>Is that the correct interpretation? I really can&#39;t see it being otherwise, but on the other hand I typically struggle to get golems in play (I often have either golems or equipment cards in my hand, but not both) and want to make sure I&#39;m not handicapping myself needlessly.</p><p>There has been the rare occasion that I can indirectly get a golem card out from Inspired Repair by playing an equipment card and then using a power to leverage that into a golem, but for me, at least, this seems to require a certain planetary alignment and possibly an act of Congress.</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
